  "id": "Compound::DB01390 - Gene::8671",
  "verbalization": "Sodium Bicarbonate is implicated in the interaction with Slc4a4 through a series of molecular mechanisms involving bicarbonate transport. The evidence suggests that Sodium Bicarbonate binds to multiple Slc4a family members, including Slc4a8, Slc4a5, and Slc4a7, which are all involved in sodium-bicarbonate symport activity. This indicates that Sodium Bicarbonate may act as a substrate or ligand for these transporters, which in turn are part of the broader bicarbonate transport pathway. The shared participation of these Slc4a members in sodium-bicarbonate symport activity suggests a common functional role in transporting bicarbonate across cellular membranes. The final scores from the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Sodium Bicarbonate and Slc4a4, likely through a shared mechanism of transport and regulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Slc4a4 in bicarbonate transport, with Sodium Bicarbonate serving as a critical component in this process.",
